# No lab configuration in operator UI (hard rule)

Operator directive (Phil, 2026-08-08), verbatim:

> **NEVER put internal lab configuration rules in UI visible to users or
> administrators. Agent/operator dialogs are not part of the product UI.
> Only generic product instructions in SPA/configurator UI — never disclose
> lab configuration (phil rotation bans, BEAVIS2, liebsoft/lanicu, seed-dev,
> Path 2 Live lab CLI recipes, SoftHSM PINs, Mailpit lab wiring, "lab
> default", etc.). Lab runbooks stay in docs/dev and agent prompts.**

**Exception** (Phil, 2026-08-08):

> **When building seed systems for developers, demo, or production, agents
> or the configurator MAY attach appropriate per-system comments that alert
> the operator for that asset's use case. Those comments are data on the
> system/asset record (a comment/notes field), shown in inventory lists —
> NOT hardcoded product Alert banners, helperText, or menu copy that embeds
> lab runbooks, CLI recipes, "never rotate phil", BEAVIS2, etc.**

## The rule

> **Product UI chrome (admin SPA, Win32/Tauri configurators, elevate
> helpers, product launchers, in-app help, Admin Manual pages shipped to
> customers) carries only generic product instructions. Internal lab host
> names, lab identities, seed recipes, SoftHSM PINs, Mailpit wiring, Path
> 2 Live CLI one-liners, phil rotation bans, and "lab default" labels
> belong in `docs/dev`, Cursor rules, and agent prompts — never in static
> Alert banners, helperText, tooltips, empty states, or menu copy.**

Agent/operator dialogs in Cursor (chat, rules, skill prompts) are **not**
product UI. That surface may name BEAVIS2, liebsoft, seed-dev, and the
rest. The SPA and shipping configurators may not hardcode those into
chrome.

## Forbidden vs allowed (chrome vs data)

| Kind | Status | Detail |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Static UI chrome** with lab configuration / internal runbooks | **Forbidden** | Hardcoded `Alert`, `helperText`, page banners, menu labels, Admin Manual prose, empty-state copy, `aria-label` strings that embed lab SOP |
| **Operator- or seed-authored `comment`** (or equivalent notes field) on inventory / system / asset rows | **Allowed** | Persisted **data** on the record; visible in MUI DataGrid (or sibling) inventory lists; editable via configurator/admin where the product supports it |
| Seed comments for **dev / demo / prod** profiles | **Allowed with care** | Must stay **use-case appropriate** for that deployment profile — alert the operator about *this asset's role* (e.g. "Modbus PLC used for OT discovery drills"). Do **not** paste agent dialog text, private lab SOP, phil bans, SoftHSM PINs, Mailpit wiring, or Path 2 Live CLI recipes into **customer production** seeds |

## Where lab detail is allowed

| Surface | Lab configuration OK? |
| --- | --- |
| `pim-offline-server/docs/dev/**`, sibling `docs/dev` | **Yes** — runbooks, RCA, preflight |
| `.cursor/rules/**`, agent skills, Task prompts | **Yes** — agent duty |
| Playwright / e2e helpers, `ui/e2e/constants.ts` | **Yes** — test fixtures, not customer chrome |
| PowerShell lab scripts under `scripts/` | **Yes** — operator/agent tooling |
| Per-row `comment` / notes on seeded or operator-edited systems | **Yes** — data, profile-appropriate (see exception) |
| Admin SPA Alert / helperText / banners / empty states / menus | **No** — static chrome |
| Win32 / Tauri configurator dialog chrome and About text | **No** — static chrome |
| In-product Admin Manual / docs pages served to admins | **No** — static chrome |
| API error messages and OpenAPI descriptions shown in UI | **No** (keep generic) |

## Forbidden in product UI chrome

Do not hardcode into toast, banner, helper text, `aria-label`, tooltip,
menu label, or Admin Manual copy any of:

| Class | Examples (non-exhaustive) |
| --- | --- |
| Lab host / seat | BEAVIS2, Beavis2, `192.168.55.197`, Docker PAM PAW lab nicknames as if product defaults |
| Lab identities | liebsoft, lanicu, "never rotate phil", phil rotation bans |
| Lab seed / restore | seed-dev, `db-init --confirm`, Restore-Beavis2Lab, Assert-Beavis2LabBaseline |
| Path / wave labels | "Path 2 Live (lab)", lab-only CLI recipes (`ot-credentials rotate-job …`) |
| SoftHSM / crypto lab | SoftHSM PINs (`2222`, `1111`), slot ids, Fix-LabSoftHsmLibraryPath |
| Messaging lab | Mailpit, `127.0.0.1:1025` / `:8025` as product instructions |
| Lab defaults | "(lab default)", "lab only", "on lab hosts" |

Generic product wording that stays allowed in chrome: "Run Discovery",
"Rotate credentials", "Use a non-personal service account for drills",
"Configure SMTP under Messaging → Email", "Select a target asset".

## Seed / inventory comments (exception detail)

1. **Shape** — Store on the system/asset (or equivalent) as `comment`,
   `notes`, or the product's existing notes column — not as a page-level
   string constant in React/Win32 resources.
2. **Display** — Inventory lists may show that field (DataGrid column,
   detail pane). That is rendering **record data**, not shipping a lab
   runbook in chrome.
3. **Authoring** — Agents building seed systems, and operators using the
   configurator/admin UI, may set comments that alert for the asset's
   use case (purpose, caution, environment role).
4. **Profile fit** — Dev/demo seeds may be more explicit about drill
   purpose. Production customer seeds must stay professional and
   non-lab: no private lab SOP, no agent chat paste, no BEAVIS2 /
   SoftHSM / Mailpit / phil-ban content.
5. **Still forbidden** — Moving a lab runbook into a comment on every
   row as a workaround for the chrome ban, or hardcoding the same lab
   paragraph into both a banner *and* a seed comment.

## Required agent behavior

1. When adding or editing SPA / configurator **chrome** copy, ask: would
   a customer admin on a non-lab host find this string confusing or
   disclosing our internal lab? If yes, move it to `docs/dev` or an
   agent rule — or, if it is truly about one asset's use case, put it
   in that asset's `comment` field instead of an Alert.
2. Keep lab identity and host rules in
   [`beavis2-lab-hard-rules.mdc`](beavis2-lab-hard-rules.mdc) and lab
   scripts — do not "help" operators by pasting those into UI banners.
3. When seeding systems, write short, profile-appropriate comments that
   help the operator understand that asset — not a dump of agent or lab
   SOP text into prod seeds.
4. Product honesty still binds
   ([`compliance-claims-honesty.mdc`](compliance-claims-honesty.mdc)):
   generic UI may say Live / Partial; it must not green-wash by citing
   lab CLI recipes as customer procedure.
5. Credibility still binds
   ([`operator-ui-credibility.mdc`](operator-ui-credibility.mdc)):
   internal slogans and lab jargon in SPA chrome look unfinished and
   cost trust — treat them as P0 copy defects.
6. Mirror this rule to `core-assets/.cursor/rules/` in the same change
   set ([`auto-commit-push.mdc`](auto-commit-push.mdc)).

## Worked violation → fix

**Violation** (OT Inventory / discovery Rotate panel, conceptual — as
shipped in `OtInventoryPage`):

```text
Path 2 Live (lab): POST /api/admin/ot/discovery/run → ot-discovery job…
Path 2 Live (lab): ot-credentials rotate-job --custody key-manager --propagate,
then AIC Server vault_bound dual-sync. … Lab only — never rotate phil.
Selected asset: (lab default)
```

A customer administrator sees internal wave labels, lab CLI recipes, the
phil ban, and "(lab default)". That is lab configuration in product UI
**chrome**.

**Fix** (generic Rotate / Discovery help — product-safe chrome):

```text
Start a discovery scan with Run Discovery. Jobs appear in the list with
status updates when the scan finishes.

Rotate credentials for the selected asset. Leave the old password empty
to rotate the password currently in effect. Prefer a dedicated service
account — do not use personal administrator accounts for rotation drills.
Select a target asset before running Rotate.
```

**Also allowed** — a seed or operator comment on a specific OT asset row,
shown in the inventory grid, e.g. for a demo seed:

```text
Demo Modbus target for OT discovery and rotate drills. Prefer the
service account on this asset; do not use personal admin accounts.
```

That comment is **data** on the row. It is not a page Alert, and a
production seed would omit lab-only naming and stay use-case clean.

Lab CLI recipes, Path 2 Live labels, phil / liebsoft / BEAVIS2, and
seed-dev steps stay in `docs/dev` and agent prompts. Sibling agents
own SPA chrome cleanup; this rule forbids reintroducing lab runbooks
into static UI strings.

